# DTF tier manifest: scan-remote-rows-gated  (artifact-keeper 1.12.0:
# #4514 plan item A3, backend PR #5071)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (Go, RubyGems,
# Composer, Pub, CocoaPods and Swift fixtures with known identities).
# LOCAL-ONLY: verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its
# pre-seeded DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: a Remote can hold `artifacts` rows of its own (replication,
# a publish into the remote, rows recorded before proxied content stopped
# being stored as rows). Before #5071 the Go, RubyGems, Composer, Pub,
# CocoaPods and Swift routes served such a row from storage without the scan
# gate, even on a fail_closed Remote that scans on proxy. Now the stored bytes
# go through the gate: a vulnerable row is 403 scan_blocked, a row whose
# archive does not back the requested coordinate is 423 under fail_closed,
# and a clean row is served 200 with X-AK-Scan: clean.
#
# The rows are seeded by pulling each fixture through an unscanned Remote and
# recording an artifacts row in the target Remotes that points at that cached
# blob (proxy-cache keys resolve at the shared storage root). The target
# Remotes' upstream is a path the mock does not serve, and the oracle checks
# it got no request, so every answer below comes from the stored row.
#
# #5076 (backend PR #5795) closes the same hole on the NuGet flat-container,
# Debian pool/, RPM package and Alpine package routes (seeded the same way
# from the mock's Newtonsoft.Json, openssl .deb, openssl-libs .rpm and busybox
# .apk fixtures, plus clean ones), and makes the generic download route
# refuse an enforced-format row of a scanning Remote with 403
# scan_on_proxy_route_required (it has no coordinate parser to grade with).
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.9 for the FIX #4514 cases; a main image after #5071
# and before #5795 (sha-d7a945a) for the FIX #5076 cases. Green: an image
# carrying artifact-keeper#5071 and #5795.
COVERS="4514 5076"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
